IMPORT prelude

-- Merchant Shipping (Civil Liability and Compensation for Bunker Oil Pollution) Act 2008 (Singapore) -- when a shipowner is
-- liable for a bunker oil spill or a threat of one (ss 2(3), 3, 4, 17(1)), who else is shielded and what environmental loss is
-- recoverable (s 5), the owner's right to limit and the insurer's (ss 6, 14(3)), pro rata distribution of a limitation fund
-- (s 7(2)), the time bar (s 11), compulsory insurance and its certificate (ss 12, 17(2)), direct action against the insurer
-- (s 14), judgments from non-Convention countries (s 16), and the offences and penalties (ss 12(6), (7), 19(2), 23(2), 27, 29(2)(e)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (the deposit's page footer reads "version in force from 1/4/2022"), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MSCLCBOPA2008.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and
-- including 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated is Act 25 of 2021 (Courts (Civil and Criminal Justice) Reform Act
-- 2021) "wef 01/04/2022", at s 17(4).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0105 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The Act is short (29 sections), so most of its operative Part 2 is here. Not encoded: the amount
-- of the limit itself (s 6(2) borrows it from s 136 of the Merchant Shipping Act 1995, not deposited with this subject), the SDR
-- conversion and claim procedure in s 7(3) to (8), ss 8 to 10 (release of arrested ships, stay of concurrent proceedings, foreign
-- funds), s 13 (the Director's discretion to issue certificates), s 15 (Admiralty jurisdiction, reciprocal enforcement), s 17(3),
-- (4) (State immunity), s 19(1) detention, ss 20 to 22, 24 to 26 and 28, the regulations power in s 12(4) to recognise further
-- certificates, and the joint liability (s 3(5)) and contributory negligence (s 3(7)) rules.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Bunker Oil Pollution Act 2008 -- liability, limitation and insurance`

-- A helper; the prelude is not relied on for a minimum.
GIVEN `first amount` IS A NUMBER, `second amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `first amount` LESS THAN `second amount` THEN `first amount` ELSE `second amount`

§§ `2(3), 3, 4 and 17(1) -- the owner's liability`

-- s 2(1): "bunker oil" means "any hydrocarbon mineral oil, including lubricating oil, used or intended to be used for the
-- operation or propulsion of a ship"; "owner" "includes the registered owner, bareboat charterer, manager and operator of the
-- ship"; "ship" means "any sea-going vessel and seaborne craft of any type". s 2(2)(a): the territory of a country includes its
-- territorial sea and exclusive economic zone.
-- s 2(3): nothing in the Act applies to "(a) any occurrence before 21 November 2008", or to a series whose first occurrence was
-- before that date.
-- s 17(1): Part 2 "does not apply in relation to any warship or any ship for the time being used by the government of any State
-- otherwise than for commercial purposes".
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD.
DECLARE Incident HAS
    `date of the first occurrence` IS A NUMBER
    `bunker oil discharged or escaped` IS A BOOLEAN
    `grave and imminent threat of contamination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `warship or non-commercial government ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ship falls under the 1998 Oil Pollution Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `bunker oil is persistent hydrocarbon mineral oil` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owner proves war or an exceptional natural phenomenon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owner proves it was wholly a stranger's act intended to do damage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owner proves it was wholly a lights authority's negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `some damage or measures in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owner acted with intent or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owner's wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `occurrence date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to an occurrence on` IF
    `occurrence date` AT LEAST 20081121

-- s 3(1): where bunker oil "is discharged or escapes from a ship, the owner of the ship shall ... be liable -- (a) for any
-- damage caused outside the ship in the territory of Singapore by contamination ...; (b) for the cost of any measures reasonably
-- taken after the discharge or escape for the purpose of preventing or minimising any damage so caused ...; and (c) for any
-- damage caused in the territory of Singapore by any measures so taken."
-- s 3(2): where there is "a grave and imminent threat of damage" (a "relevant threat of contamination") the owner is liable for
-- (a) the cost of measures reasonably taken to prevent or minimise it and (b) damage caused by those measures. There is no head
-- for contamination damage on a threat alone.
-- s 3(3): no liability for a ship to which the Merchant Shipping (Civil Liability and Compensation for Oil Pollution) Act 1998
-- applies "where that bunker oil is also persistent hydrocarbon mineral oil".
-- s 3(4): a person who incurs liability under (1) or (2) is ALSO liable as if "the territory of Singapore included the territory
-- of any other Bunker Convention country". (So damage in another Convention country rides on some liability in Singapore; and
-- s 15(2) bars an action in Singapore where there is no Singapore damage and no Singapore measures.)
-- s 4: no liability "if the owner proves" the discharge, escape or threat "(a) resulted from an act of war, hostilities, civil
-- war, insurrection or an exceptional, inevitable and irresistible natural phenomenon; (b) was due wholly to anything done or
-- left undone by another person, not being an employee or agent of the owner, with intent to do damage; or (c) was due wholly
-- to the negligence or wrongful act of a government or other authority" maintaining lights or navigational aids.
DECLARE Head IS ONE OF
    `contamination damage`
    `cost of preventive measures`
    `damage caused by preventive measures`

DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `Singapore`
    `another Bunker Convention country`
    `a non-Convention country`

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 2 applies to the incident` IF
        `the Act applies to an occurrence on` (`the incident`'s `date of the first occurrence`)
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `warship or non-commercial government ship`)

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner proves a section 4 exception` IF
        `the incident`'s `owner proves war or an exceptional natural phenomenon`
    OR  `the incident`'s `owner proves it was wholly a stranger's act intended to do damage`
    OR  `the incident`'s `owner proves it was wholly a lights authority's negligence`

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident, `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the head is open on the facts` IF
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `contamination damage` THEN `the incident`'s `bunker oil discharged or escaped`
    OTHERWISE `the incident`'s `bunker oil discharged or escaped` OR `the incident`'s `grave and imminent threat of contamination`

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident, `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is covered` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another Bunker Convention country` THEN `the incident`'s `some damage or measures in Singapore`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident, `the head` IS A Head, `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is liable for the claim` IF
        `Part 2 applies to the incident` `the incident`
    AND (NOT (`the incident`'s `ship falls under the 1998 Oil Pollution Act` AND `the incident`'s `bunker oil is persistent hydrocarbon mineral oil`))
    AND (NOT `the owner proves a section 4 exception` `the incident`)
    AND `the head is open on the facts` `the incident` `the head`
    AND `the place is covered` `the incident` `the place`

§§ `5 -- channelling and environmental loss`

-- s 5(1): whether or not the owner incurs liability under s 3, "(c) the owner shall not be liable otherwise than under that
-- section"; and "(d) no person to whom this paragraph applies shall be liable ... unless it resulted from anything done or
-- omitted to be done by the person either with intent to cause any such damage or cost or recklessly and in the knowledge that
-- any such damage or cost would probably result".
-- s 5(2): (d) applies to "(a) any servant or agent of the owner"; "(b) any person ... employed or engaged in any capacity on
-- board the ship or to perform any service for the ship"; "(c) any person performing salvage operations with the consent of the
-- owner ... or on the instructions of a competent public authority"; "(d) any person taking any of the measures" in s 3(1)(b) or
-- (2)(a); "(e) any servant or agent" of a person in (c) or (d).
-- Owner, by s 2(1), includes the registered owner, bareboat charterer, manager and operator.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the registered owner`
    `the bareboat charterer`
    `the ship manager`
    `a crew member`
    `a salvor acting with the owner's consent`
    `a clean-up contractor taking preventive measures`
    `an unconnected stranger`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `acted with intent or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is shielded from liability outside section 3` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the registered owner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the bareboat charterer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the ship manager` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an unconnected stranger` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOT `acted with intent or recklessly`

-- s 5(3): the owner's liability "for any impairment of the environment is taken to be a liability only in respect of -- (a) any
-- resulting loss of profits; and (b) the cost of any reasonable measures of reinstatement actually taken or to be taken."
DECLARE EnvironmentalLoss IS ONE OF
    `loss of profits from the impairment`
    `reasonable reinstatement measures taken or to be taken`
    `the abstract value of harm to the environment`

GIVEN `the loss` IS AN EnvironmentalLoss
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the environmental loss is recoverable` IF
    CONSIDER `the loss`
    WHEN `the abstract value of harm to the environment` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `6, 7(2), 14(3) and 16 -- limitation`

-- s 6(1): the owner "may limit that liability in accordance with and in the manner provided in section 136 of the Merchant
-- Shipping Act 1995" and the aggregate "shall not exceed the relevant amount". (2): the relevant amount is "the limit of liability
-- calculated in accordance with section 136" of that Act (not encoded: it is a parameter here).
-- s 6(4): (1) "does not apply in a case where it is proved that the discharge or escape, or the relevant threat of contamination
-- ... resulted from anything done or omitted to be done by the owner either with intent to cause any such damage or cost ... or
-- recklessly and in the knowledge that any such damage or cost would probably result".
-- s 14(3): the insurer may limit "in like manner and to the same extent as the owner" but "whether or not" the owner's conduct
-- was as mentioned in s 6(4).
GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may limit liability` IF
    NOT `the incident`'s `owner acted with intent or recklessly`

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer may limit liability` IF TRUE

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident, `total of the claims` IS A NUMBER, `the relevant amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the owner's liability after limitation` MEANS
    IF `the owner may limit liability` `the incident`
    THEN `the lesser of` `total of the claims` `the relevant amount`
    ELSE `total of the claims`

-- s 7(2)(b): the Court directs "the distribution of the amount paid into Court or to the Authority (or, as the case may be, so
-- much of it as does not exceed the liability) among those persons in proportion to their claims".
GIVEN `amount paid in` IS A NUMBER, `this claim` IS A NUMBER, `all the claims` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the claimant's share of the fund` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `amount paid in` `all the claims` TIMES `this claim` DIVIDED BY `all the claims`

-- s 16: a judgment of a court in a country "which is not a Bunker Convention country" for bunker oil pollution liability of an
-- owner in that country "may be recognised and enforced by the Court only up to the limit of liability prescribed by section 6".
GIVEN `judgment amount` IS A NUMBER, `the section 6 limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the enforceable part of a non-Convention judgment` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `judgment amount` `the section 6 limit`

§§ `11 -- time bar`

-- s 11: no action "may be entertained by any court in Singapore unless the action is commenced -- (a) not later than 3 years after
-- the claim arose; and (b) not later than 6 years after the occurrence, or first of the occurrences". Both limits must be met.
-- Periods are in years.
GIVEN `years since the claim arose` IS A NUMBER, `years since the first occurrence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is in time` IF
        `years since the claim arose` AT MOST 3
    AND `years since the first occurrence` AT MOST 6

§§ `12, 14 and 17(2) -- compulsory insurance and the insurer`

-- s 12(1): subsection (2) "applies to any ship having a gross tonnage greater than 1,000". (2): the ship "must not enter or leave
-- any port in Singapore or enter or leave any offshore facility in the territorial sea of Singapore and must not, if it is a
-- Singapore ship, enter or leave any port in any other country or any offshore facility" there, unless there is in force (a)
-- insurance or other security satisfying Article 7 of the Bunker Convention and (b) a certificate showing it.
-- s 17(1) takes warships and non-commercial government ships out of Part 2 altogether.
GIVEN `gross tonnage` IS A NUMBER, `is a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN, `uses a Singapore port or facility` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uses a foreign port or facility` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a warship or non-commercial government ship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ship needs insurance and a certificate` IF
        `gross tonnage` GREATER THAN 1000
    AND (NOT `is a warship or non-commercial government ship`)
    AND (`uses a Singapore port or facility` OR (`is a Singapore ship` AND `uses a foreign port or facility`))

-- s 12(3): the certificate shall be "(a) if the ship is a Singapore ship -- a certificate issued by the Director; (b) if the ship
-- is registered in a Bunker Convention country other than Singapore -- a certificate issued by or under the authority of the
-- government of that other Bunker Convention country; and (c) if the ship is registered in a country which is not a Bunker
-- Convention country -- a certificate issued by the Director or by or under the authority of the government of any Bunker
-- Convention country other than Singapore." (Certificates recognised by regulations under s 12(4) are not modelled.)
-- s 17(2): for a State-owned ship in commercial use, a certificate from that State's government showing State ownership and
-- that liability will be met up to the Article 7 limit is "a sufficient compliance with section 12(2)".
DECLARE Flag IS ONE OF
    `Singapore-registered`
    `registered in another Convention country`
    `registered in a non-Convention country`
    `owned by a State and in commercial use`

DECLARE Issuer IS ONE OF
    `the Director of Marine`
    `the flag State's government`
    `another Convention country's government`

GIVEN `the flag` IS A Flag, `the issuer` IS AN Issuer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is from the right issuer` IF
    CONSIDER `the flag`
    WHEN `Singapore-registered` THEN
        CONSIDER `the issuer`
        WHEN `the Director of Marine` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `registered in another Convention country` THEN
        CONSIDER `the issuer`
        WHEN `the flag State's government` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `registered in a non-Convention country` THEN
        CONSIDER `the issuer`
        WHEN `the flag State's government` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the issuer`
        WHEN `the flag State's government` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 14(1): where the owner is alleged to be liable under s 3 for an incident while certificated insurance or security was in
-- force, "proceedings to enforce a claim ... may be brought against the person who provided the insurance or other security".
-- (2): it is a defence for the insurer "(in addition to any defence affecting the owner's liability) to prove that the discharge
-- or escape or the relevant threat of contamination ... was due to the wilful misconduct of the owner".
GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident, `the head` IS A Head, `the place` IS A Place, `certificated insurance was in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant can recover from the insurer` IF
        `certificated insurance was in force`
    AND `the owner is liable for the claim` `the incident` `the head` `the place`
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `owner's wilful misconduct`)

§§ `12(6), (7), 19(2), 23(2), 27 and 29(2)(e) -- offences`

-- s 12(6): entering or leaving (or attempting to) in contravention of s 12(2) -- "the master or the registered owner" -- "a fine
-- not exceeding $1 million". (7): failing to carry or produce the certificate -- the master -- "a fine not exceeding $20,000".
-- s 19(2): a detained ship proceeding to sea before release -- the master, and the owner or sender if party or privy -- "a fine
-- not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both".
-- s 23(2): assaulting, hindering, impeding or obstructing the Director -- "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 12 months or to both".
-- s 29(2)(e): regulations may prescribe "fines not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment which may not exceed 12 months or both".
-- s 27(1): the Director may compound a prescribed compoundable offence "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding $2,000".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `using a port without insurance and certificate`
    `failing to carry or produce the certificate`
    `a detained ship going to sea`
    `obstructing the Director`
    `breaching the regulations at the statutory cap`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using a port without insurance and certificate` THEN 1000000
    WHEN `failing to carry or produce the certificate` THEN 20000
    WHEN `a detained ship going to sea` THEN 50000
    WHEN `obstructing the Director` THEN 20000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a detained ship going to sea` THEN 24
    WHEN `obstructing the Director` THEN 12
    WHEN `breaching the regulations at the statutory cap` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS 2000
